Subject: [PATCH] ggml: add GGML_TYPE_T5B -- ternary weights at 1.600 bits/weight

Adds a new CPU tensor type carrying ternary weights as base-3 digits, five per
byte: 160 weights in a 32-byte block, 1.600 bits each against i2_s's 2.000.
Lossless -- the weights are unchanged bit for bit -- with a per-tensor scale in
place of i2_s's per-block one, and an interleave identical to i2_s's so a digit
plane still addresses 32 consecutive activations.

The i2_s path is NOT touched. It is the control arm of every A/B measurement
this change is justified by, and a result measured against a moved baseline is
not a result.

Generated against, and verified to apply cleanly to:
    3rdparty/llama.cpp   390c307752ab78fd8189f359d6954c9ba1be74af
    (the submodule of microsoft/BitNet at
     0b341e582afbf9e1011f24744b554c96a3477eb5,
     from https://github.com/isHuangXin/llama.cpp.git)

This diff covers the SIX MODIFIED upstream files only. The four ADDED files --
ternary_t5b.{c,h} and ggml_t5b_glue.{c,h} -- are this repository's src/ and are
copied into ggml/src/ggml-cpu/ by integration/apply_integration.py, which also
applies these same hunks anchored rather than by line number. Use the script;
read this.

    git apply --directory=3rdparty/llama.cpp integration/t5b-integration.patch
    cp src/ternary_t5b.[ch] src/ggml_t5b_glue.[ch] \
       3rdparty/llama.cpp/ggml/src/ggml-cpu/

Apache-2.0. The modified files are MIT, Copyright (c) 2023-2024 The ggml
authors; see NOTICE.
